1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,041
What if Earth had rings like Saturn?

2
00:00:02,041 --> 00:00:05,927
From the equator, you'd see a thin, bright line running straight overhead.

3
00:00:06,417 --> 00:00:07,318
Farther north,

4
00:00:07,318 --> 00:00:12,276
they'd open into a giant arch across the sky that never moves and never sets.

5
00:00:12,276 --> 00:00:13,564
A permanent rainbow.

6
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,763
At night, sunlight still hits them, so they'd glow.

7
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:17,934
It's called ringshine.

8
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:22,425
And their shadow would fall on whichever hemisphere is having winter,

9
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:24,268
making cold seasons even colder.

10
00:00:24,783 --> 00:00:26,045
Here's the wild part.

11
00:00:26,045 --> 00:00:29,111
About four hundred and sixty-six million years ago,

12
00:00:29,111 --> 00:00:31,214
Earth may actually have had a ring.

13
00:00:31,717 --> 00:00:33,118
Full story on the channel.
